  {
    "episode_id": 91892,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91892.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 7,
    "turn_text": "I have a few priorities. First, you need money into our state, our localities, our tribal governments. We have to be able to have resources to fill these massive revenue gaps that every city and state has across the country. And that's absolutely vital for New York. I really want to prioritize our workers, our families, our hospital, small businesses, health care providers, and there's a couple of policy areas where I've really been pushing hard on. National paid leave. We want to have universal paid leave. Our second bill out of Washington only covered 25% of workers. Small workers should have up to three months paid so they can stay home with the child to school or closed so they can stay home with the loved ones who sick or care for themselves if they're sick. So if we had had paid me in place in this crisis, it would have been so much easier to manage because everyone could have stayed employed and been home for three months and still receive their pay. And we could have funded that, and that would have been simple and elegant, and no one would have lost their health care.",
