    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "So, interestingly, I think infrastructure is one of the most bipartisan ideas. But today, Mr. McConnell said he didn't want to include infrastructure in the package, which just seems backwards. Even Trump is for infrastructure, which is shocking. And infrastructure is a way to put people back to work. Anyone who's unemployed or under employed can be trained. in the building instruction trade, in the apprenticeship programs that labor offers in almost every profession. That would create a whole new generation of workers who have labor protections and skills to be able to rebuild America. So I think infrastructure should very much be part of it. I also think that some of the stuff that McConnell pushing against is not good. I mean, we're still fighting about whether we should have safety for workers and protocols for workers. They want uniform liability. So I'm very worried about that. So I'm working on that issue right now.",
