    "turn_text": "Very good, right? Racist makes more people aware that we're out there and we're giving working men and women this voice, so that would be very helpful. Okay, well, it was good to talk to you again, Kevin, and now you sound healthy and strong, so that's good. Stay safe. Thanks for listening to the Union Strong podcast. If you like what you're hearing, you can subscribe and give us a rating. This has been a production of the New York State AFL-CIO. Our president is Mario Solento. Our secretary treasurer is Terry Melvin. We're a federation of 3,000 unions representing 2.5 million union members, retirees, and their families with one goal to raise the standard of living and quality of life of all working people. We keep New York State Union strong by fighting for better wages, better benefits, and better working conditions. For more information on the labor movement in New York, visit nysaflcio.org. Until next time, stay union and stay strong.",
